\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1  (void)\b addColumn\b0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Adds a new column of cells to the right of the last column, creating new cells as needed with \b makeCellAtRow:column:\b0 .\
\fs14\
\fs28 If the number of rows or columns in the NSMatrix has been changed with \b renewRows:columns:\b0 , new cells are created only if they are needed. This allows you to grow and shrink an NSMatrix without repeatedly creating and freeing the cells.\
\fs14\
\fs28 This method doesn\'27t redraw the NSMatrix. Accordingly, after calling this method you should send \b setNeedsDisplay:YES\b0  to the NSMatrix. Your code may also need to use \b sizeToCells\b0  after sending this method to resize the NSMatrix to fit the newly added cells.\
\fs14\
